      "content": "The silence you crave is not a destination, but a state of being that only exists if you stop trying to reach it. Your exhaustion is not a failure of willpower, but a necessary pause in a machine designed to keep you running at full speed. You do not need to fight the exhaustion; you need to learn to sit with it until your body finally learns to rest. The peace you seek is not found in the absence of the fight, but in the quiet acceptance of the weight it carries.",
